# .vercelignore
# IMPORTANT: `vercel deploy` walks the filesystem itself (not just
# git-tracked files). Vercel CLI docs: once a `.vercelignore` exists, it is
# used INSTEAD of `.gitignore` — `.gitignore`'s exclusions (including
# `.env`) stop applying. This file must therefore mirror every relevant
# `.gitignore` entry itself, not just add to it.
#
# 2026-09-15 incident: adding this file without an `.env` line caused the
# next `vercel --prod` to upload the real local `.env` (DATABASE_URL,
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, NAV_TEST_* etc.) as build source — the build then
# failed for an unrelated reason before going live, but the file still
# reached Vercel's build step. Never remove the env lines below.

# --- secrets — never upload ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel

# --- dependencies / build output ---
node_modules/
dist/
web-build/
.expo/

# Nested git worktrees for concurrent Claude Code sessions/workflows — full
# checkouts (each with its own node_modules symlink) from other worktrees;
# walking into these blew the upload past Vercel's 15000-file limit (18308
# seen 2026-09-15). None of this is needed to build or serve the app.
.claude/worktrees/

# --- large non-deploy artifacts ---
docs/design/screens/
docs/audits/
e2e/
__tests__/
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/
.cursor/
.git/
